    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Half-diminished chord",
      "body": "A diminished triad with a minor 7th on top is a **half-diminished chord**. Bm7♭5 is B D F A. It is written **m7♭5** (minor 7th with a flat 5th) or with the sign **ø**: Bø.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the vii chord of a major key with its 7th, and the ii chord of a minor key. Minor-key jazz ballads lean on it for their ii–V–i.",
